---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import IndustrySection from '../../components/IndustrySection.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import QuoteCta from '../../components/QuoteCta.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';

// Copy: Content Strategist's thin-pages-copy.md. The homepage's "Who we print
// for", expanded: the same five industries in the same order, each beside a
// job we printed for one of them. Utah appears once, in the close.

const schema = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Industries', path: '/industries/' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Print for Practices, Shops, and Events"
  description="Print for dental and medical, auto, restaurants, real estate and insurance, and events. See the work, then get a free quote from DYJK Print."
  schema={schema}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Industries"
    title="Who we print for"
    subtitle="Dental and medical, auto, restaurants, real estate and insurance, events and campaigns."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-9">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <Prose>
        <p>
          Print has a person on the other end of it. A practice, a shop, a
          restaurant, a firm, or a campaign needs a piece that makes them look
          strong to their own customers. The sections below are the businesses
          we print for, each one tied to a job we have already printed. You can
          see more of that work in the <a href="/portfolio/">portfolio</a>. The
          quote is free. You approve a proof before anything prints. We ship
          anywhere in the United States.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div
    class="mx-auto max-w-6xl space-y-16 px-4 pt-14 pb-16 md:space-y-24 md:pt-18 md:pb-24"
  >
    <IndustrySection
      id="dental-and-medical"
      title="Dental and medical"
      image="presentation-folder-and-insert.jpg"
      loading="eager"
    >
      <p>
        A new patient feels the practice before anyone says hello. The folder
        they carry out, the card they keep, the brochure in the chair: that is
        the practice. Jeppson Dental, a family dental practice, needed a packet
        a new patient could take home. The folder opens onto a printed bio and a
        short list of how a visit works. A full-color insert lies across it,
        built around a photograph of a family. The logo is on the insert and on
        the folder, so the packet still names Jeppson Dental after the insert
        comes out. Practices also hand over <a href="/products/business-cards/"
          >business cards</a
        > and <a href="/products/brochures/">brochures</a> that explain a service
        without a lecture. The piece that holds it all is a <a
          href="/products/presentation-folders/">presentation folder</a
        >.
      </p>
    </IndustrySection>

    <IndustrySection
      id="auto"
      title="Auto"
      image="business-cards-despain-subaru.jpg"
      flip
    >
      <p>
        The card is the shop, the moment it changes hands. The cards we printed
        for DeSpain The Subaru Specialist are black, with a silver star and a
        blue swoosh. Two of them sit in front of a stack. The top card shows the
        DeSpain name, an engine illustration, and the line The Subaru
        Specialist. Whoever takes that card already knows the shop is the
        specialist. A <a href="/products/business-cards/">business card</a> is the
        piece they keep. A <a href="/products/flyers/">flyer</a> covers a promotion
        the shop wants seen. A <a href="/products/stickers/">sticker</a> puts the
        same name on a box or a window.
      </p>
    </IndustrySection>

    <IndustrySection
      id="restaurants"
      title="Restaurants"
      image="menus-bagel-shop.jpg"
    >
      <p>
        The menu is the meal before the first bite. The Bagel Shop needed a menu
        a guest would recognize at the table. The piece is a tall card. The
        cover is chalkboard-style: a round logo, the line "More than just a
        bagel," and the word Menu set large. That is the side a guest sees
        before any dish. <a href="/products/menus/">Restaurant menus</a> can be a
        single sheet, a fold, a tent on the table, or a takeout sheet that leaves
        with the bag. You name the one you need. A <a href="/products/flyers/"
          >flyer</a
        > can carry a special off the menu. A <a href="/products/door-hangers/"
          >door hanger</a
        > can put that special on a knob down the street. We print them. You decide
        where they go.
      </p>
    </IndustrySection>

    <IndustrySection
      id="real-estate-and-insurance"
      title="Real estate and insurance"
      image="envelopes-letterhead-apex-advance-envelopes.jpg"
      flip
    >
      <p>
        People judge the firm from the envelope, before they open it. Apex
        Insurance and Advance Insurance are two firms, each with its own
        envelope and its own logo. One carries a red and gray mountain. The
        other carries a red and gray curve along the bottom. A closed face that
        looks settled is the whole point. <a
          href="/products/envelopes-letterhead/">Envelopes and letterhead</a
        > do that job. <a href="/products/business-cards/">Business cards</a> are
        what a client keeps after the meeting. <a href="/products/door-hangers/"
          >Door hangers</a
        > are what a real estate team uses for an open house on that street. We print
        them and ship them. We do not walk the route.
      </p>
    </IndustrySection>

    <IndustrySection
      id="events-and-campaigns"
      title="Events and campaigns"
      image="flyers-atomic-auto-show.jpg"
    >
      <p>
        An event gets one sheet to explain itself. Clinch River Home Healthcare
        needed that sheet for its Atomic Auto Show. The flyer leads with a red
        headline and drawings of a classic car and a pickup. Under the art,
        three boxes divide the rest: where it is held, the entry details, and
        how to register. The logo and the website run along the bottom. A <a
          href="/products/flyers/">flyer</a
        > does that job in one sheet, handed to a person. A <a
          href="/products/door-hangers/">door hanger</a
        > stays on a knob until someone takes the invitation inside. A <a
          href="/products/postcards-mailers/">postcard</a
        > is the same news when it should arrive in the mail.
      </p>
    </IndustrySection>
  </div>

  <QuoteCta
    text="Tell us the piece and who has to notice it. The quote is free. You approve a proof before we print. We are in Utah, and we ship the finished job anywhere in the United States."
  />
</BaseLayout>
